[[:db/retract 17592186184880 :question/answer-fields 17592186183889] {:db/id 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5650e0d2-585c-5516-892d-5eacef061cb2" "question-e69dd032-aa5c-5891-a7fc-97b84703e88a" "question-fef86daf-091a-52fa-bcf0-1d2b609bb348"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184095 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Any $1\\times4$ matrix $A$ has at most $1$ singular value.\n\n- Any $4\\times2$ matrix $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n\n- The matrix ![](images/b8/b8601b1e66ef1d302e7194f262f6a513063bba2114fb063c2fc16542d4684392.svg) has one negative singular value." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-97ca7c6b-3d02-595e-9b24-0e63b350342b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184096 :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix ![](images/85/85f9ccea6cd39f07174651d07316218edf50041f9d373e22cdaedf0c779caaf3.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c791e385-b793-500d-9a77-3e468ca25a09" "question-ab4ca253-4533-55ea-9cf5-518c8864d1f6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184097 :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix ![](images/59/590d5dc32950efa0fce63a5d64a5595210a3ccb08c613e364586dba4822d7314.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5650e0d2-585c-5516-892d-5eacef061cb2" :question/id #uuid "5650e0d2-585c-5516-892d-5eacef061cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95266" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Any $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n- The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value.\n- Any $5\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 2}\\times {A}_{2\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ can't have a negative singular value.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 5}\\times {A}_{5\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-389a199b-2132-5200-92d1-2261a44348a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-389a199b-2132-5200-92d1-2261a44348a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "389a199b-2132-5200-92d1-2261a44348a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5ec6c063-a755-58f5-8636-29649c9e3395" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c2cf85b-73a0-5874-97a9-cfa33e64d6b5" "answer-e71d59cc-b53d-52ee-9d28-5a2450433b8d" "answer-4c278b14-28c2-57de-b60a-2a720876d406" "answer-5b060c6a-de3b-54b0-bfda-579bbdcbb6d0" "answer-5ec6c063-a755-58f5-8636-29649c9e3395"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c2cf85b-73a0-5874-97a9-cfa33e64d6b5" :answer/id #uuid "7c2cf85b-73a0-5874-97a9-cfa33e64d6b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e71d59cc-b53d-52ee-9d28-5a2450433b8d" :answer/id #uuid "e71d59cc-b53d-52ee-9d28-5a2450433b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c278b14-28c2-57de-b60a-2a720876d406" :answer/id #uuid "4c278b14-28c2-57de-b60a-2a720876d406" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b060c6a-de3b-54b0-bfda-579bbdcbb6d0" :answer/id #uuid "5b060c6a-de3b-54b0-bfda-579bbdcbb6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ec6c063-a755-58f5-8636-29649c9e3395" :answer/id #uuid "5ec6c063-a755-58f5-8636-29649c9e3395" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184880 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Any $6\\times 8$ matrix $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values\n- Any $10\\times 8$ matrix $A$ has at most $10$ distinct singular values.\n- The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ has two non-negative singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $6\\times 8$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $8\\times 6$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $8\\times 8$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{8\\times 6}\\times {A}_{6\\times 8}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{8\\times 8}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $10\\times 8$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $8\\times 10$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $8\\times 8$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{8\\times 10}\\times {A}_{10\\times 8}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{8\\times 8}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is true.  Indeed, all singular values of any matrix are non-negative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2360b526-d791-5f7a-b1d6-add9140e9172"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2360b526-d791-5f7a-b1d6-add9140e9172" :answer-field/id #uuid "2360b526-d791-5f7a-b1d6-add9140e9172" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7ad14134-11d1-5b66-b73a-b208f1547b8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-058c04c6-70ed-5f40-82ed-2d503073a803" "answer-7ad14134-11d1-5b66-b73a-b208f1547b8a" "answer-ef49fb2b-88b6-550b-873b-58a76d4cd449" "answer-21ea85fd-6292-5db7-9dc1-8fed164bc983" "answer-dc81e283-4f32-52f2-9dc0-2d02dfad8da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-058c04c6-70ed-5f40-82ed-2d503073a803" :answer/id #uuid "058c04c6-70ed-5f40-82ed-2d503073a803" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ad14134-11d1-5b66-b73a-b208f1547b8a" :answer/id #uuid "7ad14134-11d1-5b66-b73a-b208f1547b8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef49fb2b-88b6-550b-873b-58a76d4cd449" :answer/id #uuid "ef49fb2b-88b6-550b-873b-58a76d4cd449" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21ea85fd-6292-5db7-9dc1-8fed164bc983" :answer/id #uuid "21ea85fd-6292-5db7-9dc1-8fed164bc983" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc81e283-4f32-52f2-9dc0-2d02dfad8da9" :answer/id #uuid "dc81e283-4f32-52f2-9dc0-2d02dfad8da9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e69dd032-aa5c-5891-a7fc-97b84703e88a" :question/id #uuid "e69dd032-aa5c-5891-a7fc-97b84703e88a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95261" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Any $4\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n- The singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ are non-negative.\n- Any $3\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is true. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8cda2f1-5552-5357-82cc-f1ab61cac36e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8cda2f1-5552-5357-82cc-f1ab61cac36e" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8cda2f1-5552-5357-82cc-f1ab61cac36e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4d306b2f-e020-5c0b-8b36-318a141afa1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d306b2f-e020-5c0b-8b36-318a141afa1a" "answer-d11ab6aa-4e8f-5b94-8bb5-66fd5a8105bf" "answer-884aa6f5-9cee-5d6c-a6d2-1e3e9fda993d" "answer-f351ce40-cb01-5b7d-a5fb-a7f513b6a235" "answer-c41c10ba-d192-5a1a-9031-b8c0dab1e30f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d306b2f-e020-5c0b-8b36-318a141afa1a" :answer/id #uuid "4d306b2f-e020-5c0b-8b36-318a141afa1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d11ab6aa-4e8f-5b94-8bb5-66fd5a8105bf" :answer/id #uuid "d11ab6aa-4e8f-5b94-8bb5-66fd5a8105bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-884aa6f5-9cee-5d6c-a6d2-1e3e9fda993d" :answer/id #uuid "884aa6f5-9cee-5d6c-a6d2-1e3e9fda993d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f351ce40-cb01-5b7d-a5fb-a7f513b6a235" :answer/id #uuid "f351ce40-cb01-5b7d-a5fb-a7f513b6a235" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c41c10ba-d192-5a1a-9031-b8c0dab1e30f" :answer/id #uuid "c41c10ba-d192-5a1a-9031-b8c0dab1e30f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fef86daf-091a-52fa-bcf0-1d2b609bb348" :question/id #uuid "fef86daf-091a-52fa-bcf0-1d2b609bb348" :question/math-academy-id "q-95281" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Any $6\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n- The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value.\n- Any $4\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $6\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 6}\\times {A}_{6\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ can't have a negative singular value.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d97b8052-bb1d-524c-878a-c0e3b532b8c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d97b8052-bb1d-524c-878a-c0e3b532b8c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "d97b8052-bb1d-524c-878a-c0e3b532b8c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f25d7873-4bce-5acd-bc01-3466707919a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4727adce-5afb-5a6e-baec-86299311d447" "answer-f25d7873-4bce-5acd-bc01-3466707919a3" "answer-9d9dee5f-cd09-5188-9a3c-cde7f4e68a37" "answer-4ab592cf-fe9a-5d31-b42c-37ad02aab55a" "answer-862c188a-6765-5375-b045-c13862731467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4727adce-5afb-5a6e-baec-86299311d447" :answer/id #uuid "4727adce-5afb-5a6e-baec-86299311d447" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f25d7873-4bce-5acd-bc01-3466707919a3" :answer/id #uuid "f25d7873-4bce-5acd-bc01-3466707919a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d9dee5f-cd09-5188-9a3c-cde7f4e68a37" :answer/id #uuid "9d9dee5f-cd09-5188-9a3c-cde7f4e68a37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ab592cf-fe9a-5d31-b42c-37ad02aab55a" :answer/id #uuid "4ab592cf-fe9a-5d31-b42c-37ad02aab55a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-862c188a-6765-5375-b045-c13862731467" :answer/id #uuid "862c188a-6765-5375-b045-c13862731467" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-97ca7c6b-3d02-595e-9b24-0e63b350342b" :question/id #uuid "97ca7c6b-3d02-595e-9b24-0e63b350342b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95367" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}17-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -8 & 17-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (17-\\lambda )(17-\\lambda )-64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-34\\lambda +289-64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-34\\lambda +225 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{9}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-186b2a25-d332-5f01-a6a2-293d5802ee3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-186b2a25-d332-5f01-a6a2-293d5802ee3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "186b2a25-d332-5f01-a6a2-293d5802ee3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4f699d44-55da-5c4f-a3d1-373644f33ba8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-514af78b-310e-50a2-b1ef-8f945c043cb2" "answer-b85ee86c-0aac-52bc-b5db-5824de7a6bdc" "answer-392bfe36-8b63-5aac-ad95-fe5e63ae7b56" "answer-4f699d44-55da-5c4f-a3d1-373644f33ba8" "answer-2c448a4f-2853-5a0a-adb6-34c3fe973ba2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-514af78b-310e-50a2-b1ef-8f945c043cb2" :answer/id #uuid "514af78b-310e-50a2-b1ef-8f945c043cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b85ee86c-0aac-52bc-b5db-5824de7a6bdc" :answer/id #uuid "b85ee86c-0aac-52bc-b5db-5824de7a6bdc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25$ and $9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-392bfe36-8b63-5aac-ad95-fe5e63ae7b56" :answer/id #uuid "392bfe36-8b63-5aac-ad95-fe5e63ae7b56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f699d44-55da-5c4f-a3d1-373644f33ba8" :answer/id #uuid "4f699d44-55da-5c4f-a3d1-373644f33ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c448a4f-2853-5a0a-adb6-34c3fe973ba2" :answer/id #uuid "2c448a4f-2853-5a0a-adb6-34c3fe973ba2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c791e385-b793-500d-9a77-3e468ca25a09" :question/id #uuid "c791e385-b793-500d-9a77-3e468ca25a09" :question/math-academy-id "q-95359" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda -5\\lambda +40-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd7054d7-ed2b-5613-b2fc-90c17c4791c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd7054d7-ed2b-5613-b2fc-90c17c4791c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7054d7-ed2b-5613-b2fc-90c17c4791c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" "answer-b8b05a8d-1f8d-58ee-8ab2-e2cf7750d0f9" "answer-e93e9e61-f7d3-5cb6-85a3-a9059ed558a7" "answer-a08ff49c-3e48-5969-9cc0-4603170a0646" "answer-c7d2dbc4-67b2-5124-9e27-6ec2f6fd08b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer/id #uuid "4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8b05a8d-1f8d-58ee-8ab2-e2cf7750d0f9" :answer/id #uuid "b8b05a8d-1f8d-58ee-8ab2-e2cf7750d0f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e93e9e61-f7d3-5cb6-85a3-a9059ed558a7" :answer/id #uuid "e93e9e61-f7d3-5cb6-85a3-a9059ed558a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a08ff49c-3e48-5969-9cc0-4603170a0646" :answer/id #uuid "a08ff49c-3e48-5969-9cc0-4603170a0646" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7d2dbc4-67b2-5124-9e27-6ec2f6fd08b3" :answer/id #uuid "c7d2dbc4-67b2-5124-9e27-6ec2f6fd08b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab4ca253-4533-55ea-9cf5-518c8864d1f6" :question/id #uuid "ab4ca253-4533-55ea-9cf5-518c8864d1f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-139508" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{9}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-533bf985-e003-5103-b11c-9c7a7c723cb4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-533bf985-e003-5103-b11c-9c7a7c723cb4" :answer-field/id #uuid "533bf985-e003-5103-b11c-9c7a7c723cb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c2115b7-3deb-582b-a761-e79b45a72ba3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-872eaed5-b7dd-5088-8dd0-359491c4f657" "answer-3c2115b7-3deb-582b-a761-e79b45a72ba3" "answer-72a19815-f7b7-56e9-badf-ea7b9e73091b" "answer-949e815d-00ae-5171-94b0-1798b1a30df1" "answer-93dcd708-1476-51b0-ac1f-9db7ca101165"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-872eaed5-b7dd-5088-8dd0-359491c4f657" :answer/id #uuid "872eaed5-b7dd-5088-8dd0-359491c4f657" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3,$ $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c2115b7-3deb-582b-a761-e79b45a72ba3" :answer/id #uuid "3c2115b7-3deb-582b-a761-e79b45a72ba3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3,$ $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72a19815-f7b7-56e9-badf-ea7b9e73091b" :answer/id #uuid "72a19815-f7b7-56e9-badf-ea7b9e73091b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6,$ $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-949e815d-00ae-5171-94b0-1798b1a30df1" :answer/id #uuid "949e815d-00ae-5171-94b0-1798b1a30df1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9,$ $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93dcd708-1476-51b0-ac1f-9db7ca101165" :answer/id #uuid "93dcd708-1476-51b0-ac1f-9db7ca101165" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9,$ $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185322 :tutorial/content "Recall that the singular values of a real matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix $A^T \\! A.$\n\nAlso, since $A^T \\! A$ is a positive semi-definite matrix, the eigenvalues of $A^T \\! A$ must be always non-negative real numbers.\n\nLet's compute the singular values of the matrix $A,$ given by \n\n![](images/a9/a9edbe1fee59758c9557d95ea8f62468f9f3cb98449c437a274bdbf5c30f7dc6.svg)\n\nNow, since\n\n- $A$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix, and\n\n- $A^T$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix,\n\nthen $A^T \\! A$  must be a $2 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2} \\times {\\large 3}}{A^T} \\times \\underset{{\\large 3} \\times \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2}}{A} = \n\\underset{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2} \\times \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{\\large 2}}{A^T \\! A}\n$$\n\nLet's now compute our singular values. First, we calculate $A^T \\! A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\,0 & \\,2 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}\\,0 & \\,2 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,0 & \\,2 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the eigenvalues of $A^T \\! A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When listing the singular values of a matrix, we usually write them in descending order.\n\n- If $A$ is a $m\\times n$ matrix, then $A^T A$ is a $n\\times n$ positive semi-definite matrix. This means that $A$ has *at most* $n$ distinct singular values." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184404 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
